Investigate a material or component failure with competing causal explanations and validated correction (@metal-failure-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @metals-and-metallurgical-production, #source "../sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC", #source "../sources/Rockwell-Hardness-Measurement-NIST.lingua#r_00QNYTS0KD4Y8SCJR68K1JECFM", #source "../sources/Charpy-Impact-Uncertainty-NIST.lingua#r_5GBY4J4HZTHJSY48TSH3RZ0MZR", #source "../sources/Nondestructive-Testing-Training-Guidelines-IAEA.lingua#r_7BCDSPEZ4HRMK7C1WPARVR2AP7", #source "../sources/ASM-Mechanical-Testing-and-Evaluation.lingua#r_1VW327STC5YQGRAPNRAPQSZQNG", #source "../sources/ASM-Metallography-and-Microstructures.lingua#r_4XHEJ1ZHW0B1YNG9AWCEC491ME", #metals-and-metallurgical-production "Integrated-feed-to-qualified-metal-product-and-recovery-study.lingua#r_23EJ948P4NHVC4SFAK06ERMSGF") { r_6GM4DMN4X8E248D3HPH49BM2JE
**Read:** [Mechanical Behavior of Materials — Krystyn Van Vliet, MIT 3.22](../sources/Mechanical-Behavior-MIT-3-22.lingua#r_53J3ZM414SJR3SFW7Q1G8ZJWDC), the entire graduate programme and research/special-topic work; [Rockwell Hardness Measurement of Metallic Materials — Samuel R. Low, NIST](../sources/Rockwell-Hardness-Measurement-NIST.lingua#r_00QNYTS0KD4Y8SCJR68K1JECFM), the full guide where hardness evidence is used; [Computing Uncertainty for Charpy Impact Machine Test Results — NIST](../sources/Charpy-Impact-Uncertainty-NIST.lingua#r_5GBY4J4HZTHJSY48TSH3RZ0MZR), the full guide where impact evidence is used; [Training Guidelines in Non-destructive Testing Techniques — IAEA, revision 3](../sources/Nondestructive-Testing-Training-Guidelines-IAEA.lingua#r_7BCDSPEZ4HRMK7C1WPARVR2AP7), the complete common and applicable method guidance; [Mechanical Testing and Evaluation — ASM Handbook, volume 8](../sources/ASM-Mechanical-Testing-and-Evaluation.lingua#r_1VW327STC5YQGRAPNRAPQSZQNG), whole applicable test/evaluation chapters, when available; [Metallography and Microstructures — ASM Handbook, volume 9](../sources/ASM-Metallography-and-Microstructures.lingua#r_4XHEJ1ZHW0B1YNG9AWCEC491ME), whole applicable preparation/interpretation chapters, when available.

Complete the full graduate mechanical-behavior work and original special-topic study. Select a documented failure/performance problem with sufficiently preserved material identity, manufacturing/service history, geometry/loading, environment, observation methods, and uncertainty. Read whole relevant professional/technical methods and complete primary investigation and comparison papers.

Develop competing causal accounts before selecting tests. Combine nondestructive/dimensional, chemical, metallographic/crystallographic, fractographic, mechanical, and environmental evidence as appropriate. Preserve what each sample/preparation changes and distinguish observed damage from inferred initiating events and later consequences.

Independently reproduce substantial mechanics, chemistry/transport, structure, or uncertainty calculations and check applicability/validity limits. Validate the preferred explanation against independent material regions, service states, or controlled comparisons. Explain missing history and observations that remain compatible with more than one mechanism.

**Work:** defend a corrective material/process/design, inspection, or maintenance arrangement and a test that could demonstrate whether it addresses the causal problem without creating a consequential new one. Compare uncertainty and changed service conditions rather than declaring success from one favorable coupon. Produce an inspectable evidence chain another team can challenge, reproduce, and use to continue the material and working-system investigation.

**Continue:** [Construct a coherent metal-production, use-quality, and recovery study across the whole chain](Integrated-feed-to-qualified-metal-product-and-recovery-study.lingua#r_23EJ948P4NHVC4SFAK06ERMSGF).

**Return:** [Metals and metallurgical production — feed, refining, structure, useful products, and recovery](../Metals-and-metallurgical-production.lingua#r_59BDAQXT81552YF5F8TH4KQQH1).
